## 1. Project Title & Problem Statement

**Title:** Sunlight & Shadow Analyzer (SSA) — interactive sun-path, shadow, and sunlight-hours tool for small-site planning.

**Problem:** A junior urban planner or architecture student working on small urban plots in a dense city like Lahore cannot quickly see how a proposed building changes sunlight on neighbouring courtyards, rooftops, and gardens over a whole day. Professional tools (Ecotect, SketchUp plugins, GIS suites) are heavy, licensed, or online-only; hand-drawn shadow diagrams show only one or two instants, so a layout's worst hours are easy to miss. **Solution:** a fully offline Python/tkinter app where she drags box buildings onto a ground plane, scrubs a time/date slider to watch the sun and shadows move in real time, runs a sunlight-hours heatmap, and compares two layouts (before/after) with numeric and visual differences. All assumptions and uncertainty are disclosed in the interface.

