## 2. Success Criteria

Testable via Help → "Run self-tests", Help → "Benchmark", or the manual checklist in §10.

- **SC1 Solar accuracy.** For the five reference cases in §10.1, computed azimuth and elevation fall within stated tolerances (±2°–±4° azimuth, ±1° elevation). Self-test pass rate = 100 %.
- **SC2 Shadow direction and length.** Lahore (31.5204° N, 74.3587° E, UTC+5), 2024-03-21 at 10:00 local: sun azimuth 129° ± 2°, elevation 46.3° ± 1.5°; ground shadow of a 10 m wall points along 309° ± 2°; length 9.6 m ± 0.6 m (L = H / tan(el)).
- **SC3 Responsiveness.** 15 buildings, 30×30 grid, slider dragged across full range: p95 redraw ≤ 66 ms (≥ 15 FPS), measured over 100 redraws by the built-in benchmark.
- **SC4 Task time.** 5-person pilot: ≥ 4/5 add a building and state its shadow direction within 30 s; ≥ 4/5 drag a building to a new cell within 5 s.
- **SC5 Heatmap speed.** Defaults (15 buildings, 15-min step, full day): "Run heatmap" finishes in ≤ 5 s pure Python. Progress bar updates ≥ 5×/s, no freeze > 200 ms, Cancel effective ≤ 0.5 s.
- **SC6 Heatmap correctness.** Unoccluded cell matches independent 1-minute scan within ±0.25 h (≈ 11.8 h for Lahore 2024-03-21, elevation threshold 2°). Cell 2 m north of centre of a 20 m × 30 m wall on 2024-12-21 shows 0.0 h.
- **SC7 Comparison integrity.** Displayed Δ = Σ(B−A) over common free cells within 1e-6 h. 20 consecutive compare toggles: no exception, each ≤ 1 s. Stale indicator appears ≤ 100 ms after any edit.
- **SC8 Disclosure and accessibility.** Assumptions dialog ≤ 2 clicks, ≥ 6 assumptions listed. Legend swatch colours equal rendered cell colours (automated check). All text/background pairs meet WCAG ≥ 4.5:1. Every heatmap value readable via hover. Every control reachable by Tab; selected building movable by arrow keys.

