## 3. Scope

### 3.1 In scope

**Tier 1 (must-have)**
- Box buildings with add, move (mouse drag), move (arrow keys), **height adjustment via spinbox**, recolour, delete. Footprint size (width × depth) is chosen **only at creation and cannot be changed afterward**. Footprints snap to 2 m grid; overlaps rejected. Max 15 buildings.
- NOAA solar azimuth/elevation from lat, lon, date, time, user-supplied timezone offset, with sunrise/sunset estimates.
- Isometric canvas with painter's-algorithm depth ordering and flat Lambertian face shading. Live ground shadows update while scrubbing time slider.
- Month/day/year date picker, lat/lon/tz entries, city preset list.
- "Run heatmap": direct sunlight hours for ground cells and building roofs for the selected day. Non-blocking, cancellable, with progress bar. Legend, hover readout, stale indicator included.
- A/B comparison as side-by-side panes (small multiples). Difference heatmap and metric panel (total change, percent change, cells gained/lost, area fraction ≥ target hours threshold).
- Compass rose with sun-azimuth marker, status bar, Assumptions & Limits dialog, JSON save/load, built-in self-tests and benchmark.

**Tier 2 (only after Tier 1 passes)**
Facade heatmap. Lambertian cosine-weighted accumulation view. Multi-day range. View rotation in ±90° steps. Sunrise/Noon/Sunset quick-jumps, ±15 min step buttons, play/animate. Undo/redo (20 levels, JSON snapshots). Optional numpy-vectorised heatmap path with identical results (±1e-6).

### 3.2 Explicitly OUT of scope (do not build)

1. No full 3D renderer, perspective camera, OpenGL, z-buffer, or ray-traced image.
2. No non-box geometry (sloped roofs, cylinders, OBJ/CAD imports, courtyard cutouts).
3. No building rotation (all boxes axis-aligned).
4. No terrain, slopes, vegetation, trees.
5. No weather, clouds, atmospheric attenuation, irradiance models, kWh/PV yield.
6. No reflections, indirect/diffuse sky light, ambient occlusion, soft penumbra. Hard-edged shadows, point sun only.
7. No timezone database, DST rules, geocoding, online map/city search. Timezone offset always user-provided.
8. No PNG/PDF/image export, printing, networking, accounts, cloud sync, multi-user.
9. No localisation, no mobile/web build.
10. No third-party libraries beyond optional numpy. No imports of `dataclasses`, `typing`, `copy`, `sys`, `os`, `time`, `random`.

